{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES-REQUESTED at exact clean head afbb9dd80a52d0d1423ca782703be1874bfbecdf, artifact 828dd6bc1c843b7935d0ac76e57adcb21ac4f5cc.\n\nThe fold distinctions, satisfied terminality, honest profile-marker wording, ten-status documentation, replacement-promise wording, and rebuilt served bundle are good. Two blockers remain.\n\n1. `released` is still classified as closed as well as attention. I initially said this made the row disappear; that was too strong because filterWorkProjection includes active OR attention OR closed, so the default attention filter keeps the row visible. The remaining defect is semantic and measurable: workItemState returns closed=true, every closed count includes it, the Closed-only filter includes it, and the test still calls it a terminal lifecycle and still says the request wants a new performer. A released promise leaves the signed request live and awaiting a replacement promise from the same addressed actor. Remove released from CLOSED_WORK_STATUSES, correct that test and comment, and add a direct projection/default-filter assertion proving released is attention-visible, not closed, and not actionable. Revoked may remain closed+attention because the request itself was retired by authority.\n\n2. The changed behavior documentation is still anchored to predecessor behavior. docs/concepts/work-loop.md, docs/reference/gs/status.md, docs/reference/mcp/work.md, and docs/reference/mcp/status.md retain their old rests_on sets; none cites the current fold/statusview/MCP behavior represented by this head. Artifact 828dd6 names only internal/workroom and still reports one live predecessor with succession_unrecorded. Record the current behavior artifacts for every changed behavior path, settle their predecessors, then make a docs-only exact-head commit re-anchoring the four pages and record page artifacts there. Request review of that new exact head. Do not replace unchanged behavior artifacts merely because the docs-only head